{"id": "EUVD-2026-82170", "enisaUuid": "d3a51b8a-1b67-3b92-96c2-f5271a901ee0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm/adreno: fix use after free on error path in a6xx_gpu_init()\n\nThe a6xx_destroy() function frees \"a6xx_gpu\" and so \"adreno_gpu\" points\nto freed memory.  Preserve the error code before freeing the memory to\navoid a use after free.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/732275/", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/105aaff286a153bfde3c1f5be534e6ded1f64342", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8a9c9c5787bed1243e5364c89ca66c26b4e4d83"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93060", "GHSA-m3w8-h85h-3vf3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "031eafa2-c04f-3b9e-97e8-52cc9898efc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1d619000-c472-3288-aa19-49bdd59de1a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.2"}, {"id": "673e94f7-0c8f-3a50-806a-c8da39772bb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d158886cba08688f2d8d0dbb7025a4440e6a8ffd <b8a9c9c5787bed1243e5364c89ca66c26b4e4d83"}, {"id": "715d2dda-a6e1-3cd2-a47d-c23bea66d41f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "75074fc0-113f-3734-ba4c-3f7d219af6ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d158886cba08688f2d8d0dbb7025a4440e6a8ffd <105aaff286a153bfde3c1f5be534e6ded1f64342"}, {"id": "9b2fcf8c-3070-3b00-966f-0049c4db4c7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5de853df-0f5b-3c0f-be42-b4d03197798a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}